+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "22",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Example 2) Usage for Custom Function Optimization"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "23",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "We can define a domain with input features, and constraints. Output features are not required"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "24",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "domain = domains_data_models.Domain(\n",
+    "    inputs=domains_data_models.Inputs(\n",
+    "        features=[\n",
+    "            features_data_models.ContinuousInput(\n",
+    "                key=\"x_1\",\n",
+    "                bounds=(-6, 6),\n",
+    "            ),\n",
+    "            features_data_models.ContinuousInput(\n",
+    "                key=\"x_2\",\n",
+    "                bounds=(-6, 6),\n",
+    "            ),\n",
+    "        ]\n",
+    "    ),\n",
+    "    constraints=[\n",
+    "        constraints_data_models.NonlinearInequalityConstraint(\n",
+    "            expression=\"x_1**2 + x_2**2 - 16\",\n",
+    "            features=[\"x_1\", \"x_2\"],\n",
+    "        ),\n",
+    "    ],\n",
+    ")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "25",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "optimizer = strategies_data_models.GeneticAlgorithmOptimizer(\n",
+    "    population_size=100,\n",
+    "    n_max_gen=100,\n",
+    "    verbose=False,\n",
+    ")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "26",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "### Define the optimization problem: a) Using evaluations on `pd.DataFrame` \n",
+    "We want to maximize the mean variance of the experiments dataframe. The objective function will be called with a list of dataframes, each representing a set of experiments. Each list entry is one individual in the population of the GA.\n",
+    "The direction of the optimizer is a minimization of the objective function. So we minimize the negative mean variance of each 3 experiments in a batch in this case."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "27",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "def objective_function(x: List[pd.DataFrame]) -> np.ndarray:\n",
+    "    \"\"\"assume we want to maximize the mean variance of the experiments dataframe\"\"\"\n",
+    "    vars = [xi.var(numeric_only=True).mean() for xi in x]\n",
+    "    return -np.array(vars)"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "28",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "Run the optimization with the utility function `run_ga`"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "29",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "x_opt, f_opt = run_ga(\n",
+    "    data_model=optimizer,\n",
+    "    domain=domain,\n",
+    "    objective_callables=[objective_function],  # list of objective functions to optimize\n",
+    "    q=3,  # number of points to optimize\n",
+    "    callable_format=\"pandas\",\n",
+    ")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "30",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "data": {
+      "text/html": [
+       "<div>\n",
+       "<style scoped>\n",
+       "    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n",
