+    "plt.figure(figsize=(4, 4))\n",
+    "plt.plot(proposals[\"x_1\"], proposals[\"x_2\"], \"o\", label=\"Proposals\")\n",
+    "x = np.linspace(-4, 4, 100)\n",
+    "y1 = np.sqrt(16 - x**2)\n",
+    "y2 = -y1\n",
+    "plt.plot(x, y1, \"r--\", label=\"x_1**2 + x_2**2 <= 4\")\n",
+    "plt.plot(x, y2, \"r--\")\n",
+    "plt.xlim(-6, 6)\n",
+    "plt.ylim(-6, 6)\n",
+    "plt.legend()\n",
+    "plt.show()"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "32",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "### Define the optimization problem: a) Using evaluations on `torch.Tensor`\n",
+    "For efficiency, we can also compute the objective function as a callable of type `Tensor`. In this case, the computation is in the *numerical domain*. \n",
+    "\n",
+    "This means, that categorical columns etc. are encoded. A specification with `input_preprocessing_specs` can be passed to the objective function (otherwise, defaults are used)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The objective accepts a Tensor in shape (n, q, d) and should return a Tensor of shape (n,)   "
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "33",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "def objective_function(x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n",
+    "    var = torch.var(x, dim=2)\n",
+    "    var_mean = torch.mean(var, dim=1)\n",
+    "    return var_mean"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "34",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "x_opt, f_opt = run_ga(\n",
+    "    data_model=optimizer,\n",
+    "    domain=domain,\n",
+    "    objective_callables=[objective_function],  # list of objective functions to optimize\n",
+    "    q=3,  # number of points to optimize\n",
+    "    callable_format=\"torch\",\n",
+    ")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "35",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
